      "category": "bug",
      "title": "Retry after a worker crash charges the card twice",
      "body": "Step 4 calls ChargeCard and then writes the ledger row in a separate transaction. The retry policy in step 6 re-runs the whole job on any failure. A crash between the charge and the ledger write leaves no record of the charge, so the retry charges again.",
      "failure_scenario": "Worker is OOM-killed right after ChargeCard returns; the job is retried 30s later and the customer is charged 2x for invoice INV-20931.",
      "suggestion": "Pass invoice.ID as the provider idempotency key and write a pending ledger row before the charge; the retry reads it and resumes instead of charging.",
      "confidence": 9
    },
